{
  "id": "29164_kaeru",
  "headword": "{返|かえ}る",
  "reading": "かえる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (intransitive)",
  "gloss": "to return; to be returned; to revert",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to return; to be returned; to come back",
      "explanation": "Of something borrowed, lent, or taken — to come back to its owner or original place. Often used with きた to mean something has come back."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to revert; to return to a previous state",
      "explanation": "To go back to a former condition, such as consciousness returning, a situation reverting, or something going back to normal."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29164_kaeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{貸|か}した{本|ほん}がやっと{返|かえ}ってきた。",
      "english": "The book I lent finally came back.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29164_kaeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{敷金|しききん}の{一部|いちぶ}が{返|かえ}ってきた。",
      "english": "Part of the security deposit was returned.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29164_kaeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{投資|とうし}したお{金|かね}が{返|かえ}ってくる{保証|ほしょう}はない。",
      "english": "There is no guarantee that the money invested will come back.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29164_kaeru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{意識|いしき}が{返|かえ}った。",
      "english": "Consciousness returned.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29164_kaeru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{話|はなし}が{元|もと}に{返|かえ}ってしまった。",
      "english": "The conversation reverted to square one.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29164_kaeru_ex6",
      "japanese": "{手術|しゅじゅつ}を{受|う}けたあと、{体|からだ}が{元|もと}の{状態|じょうたい}に{返|かえ}るまでに{時間|じかん}がかかった。",
      "english": "After surgery, it took time for the body to return to its original state.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- {返|かえ}る (intransitive): something returns/comes back on its own\n- {返|かえ}す: to return something; to give back (transitive counterpart)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {返|かえ}ってくる: to come back (emphasizes movement toward the speaker)\n- {元|もと}に{返|かえ}る: to revert; to go back to how it was\n- {意識|いしき}が{返|かえ}る: consciousness returns\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {帰|かえ}る: to return home, to go back (used for people returning to a place)\n- {戻|もど}る: to return; to come back — broader and more common in everyday speech",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
